ame></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYA, KAZUYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UESUGI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASAPIDIS MAKIS</name><address><country>GB</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITAGAWA KEIICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYA KAZUYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UESUGI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASAPIDIS, MAKIS</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITAGAWA, KEIICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYA, KAZUYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UESUGI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A reception quality measurement section (108) measures the reception quality, a bit judging section (111) judges whether the TPC bit is 0 or 1, an amplitude reading section (112) reads the ratio of the amplitude of the signal other than the TPC bit to that of the TPC, a cumulating section (113) judges the change and changed amount of the transmission power on the assumption that the code of the TPC bit is a change of the transmission power and that the amplitude ratio is the changed amount of transmission power and gives a transmission amplifier (104) an instruction, and a multiplying section (114) multiplies the amplitude of the signal other than the TPC bit by a correction value corresponding to the reception quality and determines the amplitude of the TPC bit.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un module (108) d'évaluation de la qualité de réception, un module (111) qui juge si le bit TPC est de 0 ou 1, un module (112) qui fait une lecture du rapport entre l'amplitude du signal du bit non TPC sur l'amplitude du signal du bit TPC, un module (113) de cumul qui évalue la modification et la quantité modifiée de puissance de transmission selon l'hypothèse que le code du bit TPC est une modification de la puissance de transmission et que le rapport d'amplitude est la quantité modifiée de puissance de transmission, et donne à l'amplificateur (104) de transmission une instruction, et un module (114) qui multiplie l'amplitude du signal du bit non TPC par une valeur de correction correspondant à la qualité de réception et détermine l'amplitude du bit TPC.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>